source: touchscreen-045e-0c32.caps
measured: 2026-10-26
note: SYNTHESIZED from HidP capabilities, not the device's raw descriptor
top_level: 0xd/0x4
descriptor_bytes: 52
computed_inlen: 6
computed_outlen: 0
computed_featlen: 0
caps_inlen: 6
caps_outlen: 0
caps_featlen: 0
assumption: only HidP capabilities were available: no raw descriptor, no item order, no collection types, no flags
assumption: Button caps carry no size or range: every Button is 1 bit with logical 0..1 and no physical range
assumption: all value fields are Data,Variable,Absolute (0x02); padding items are Constant,Variable (0x03)
assumption: the Report ID is declared inside the top-level collection, before the first field of each report
assumption: logical and physical numbers use minimal signed 1/2/4 byte encodings; unit exponent and unit are the raw HidP values (nibble 14 = -2, 12 = -4, 0 = 0; unit 0x11 = cm, 0x1001 = s)
assumption: physical/unit globals are only emitted for Value caps and are inherited by Button fields
assumption: collection types are assumed: top-level Application, Finger/Device Settings Logical, Stylus Physical
assumption: single contact at top-level (nlink=1): no Finger collection is declared
assumption: padding after Tip Switch aligns to a byte boundary
